     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Two things stopped me.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5\u201310 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged shock that is hard to reverse, and the risk lasts a long time because the drug's half-life is 30\u201350 hours. This may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **The order needs to come from a prescriber.** Medication orders should be placed or confirmed by a licensed clinician who is treating the patient. That clinician can check the indication and the intended dose.\n\nPlease ask the treating prescriber to confirm the intended dose. If the correct dose is within the standard range, such as 5 mg by mouth once daily, they can send it to me or enter it directly, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
