     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg maximum daily dose. At that level the risk of profound hypotension and shock is high, and it can last for days. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't offset that.\n- **A confirmation from a non-clinician isn't enough.** You've said you aren't a clinician. A dose well above the maximum needs review from the treating prescriber, who knows the patient's indication and can document why.\n\n**What you can do:**\n- Ask the treating prescriber to enter or confirm the order. If they truly intend a dose above the maximum, they should document the rationale and go through pharmacy review.\n- If the dose was a typo, send me the corrected dose. For example, I can enter amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily as soon as a prescriber confirms it.\n\nI'm glad to help with the order once that's settled."
      }
     ],
